  "databases": {
    "control": "PostgreSQL 17, isolated Hibernate schemas using Spring HibernateJpaVendorAdapter settings",
    "targets": [
      "PostgreSQL 17",
      "MySQL 8.4"
    ],
    "containersRemoved": true
  },
  "checks": [
    "Version-two intents freeze complete per-model resource-code maps: binding identity, optional projection identity, owner, generation and projected model. Empty maps and legacy missing projections are explicit. The old scalar generation is required to be zero, never used as a maximum or substituted model version.",
    "Version-one canonical bytes retain the pre-change pinned SHA-256 b09ae08f07e43bd7ced93c93cc49a93e9251325331b96807c9e4fa9ba3fa01cf. Version-two storage round trips strict canonical JSON; fractional generations, mixed versions, missing/wrong model scopes, wrong owners and duplicated binding identities are refused. Nested snapshots are immutable.",
    "The metadata resolver requires a joined control transaction and managed live tenant model write locks. Bounded scalar queries read current resources without acquiring resource locks after model locks. Revoked and foreign-tenant bindings are excluded; active bindings to formally offline projections fail closed.",
    "Actual PostgreSQL control metadata is composed with each real target DB. Changing a lower resource generation from 3 to 4 is detected although another resource remains at generation 9; unbinding an owned-model resource also invalidates the frozen snapshot.",
    "The coordinator commits maintenance claim before calculation. Subsequent attempts preserve the original command, clock, actor and installed-definition identity, even when called by a different trusted recovery actor.",
    "Each attempt uses a new READ_COMMITTED control transaction, sorted model locks, fresh metadata and a bounded borrowed target transaction. The metadata/lock elapsed time is deducted before assigning the target budget.",
    "Management projection changes are refused while the composed publication is nonterminal. Idempotent binding of a legacy resource and unbinding a missing resource also roll back newly created projection rows, preserving the frozen resource association.",
    "The coordinator performs full real staging, application and activation. Terminal replay succeeds after later resource generations and policy revisions, without replacing the original intent or modifying records again.",
    "A replacement publication freezes a non-null previously installed calculation policy. After its candidate rows are applied, cancellation restores complete physical parent/child snapshots and preserves that original installed policy while consuming the target revision.",
    "A runtime calculation failure after claim persists a stable diagnostic in a separate guarded attempt with sequence CAS and no business changes. Cancellation then releases maintenance while retaining the previous policy and exact original data.",
    "A delayed publish request after restoration starts is rejected without changing restoration progress or inventing a restoration failure.",
    "Full DNA API/implementation/service regressions pass, including the earlier two-order control/target contention tests and target batch fault scenarios; no failures/errors/skips and no main implementation Checkstyle findings."
  ],
  "correctedFindings": [
    {
      "defect": "A scalar resource generation lacks the resource identity and cannot safely represent multiple page bindings.",
      "fix": "A versioned immutable resource-association snapshot is read under model locks and checked in full before every nonterminal batch/cancellation decision."
    },
    {
      "defect": "Legacy bind/unbind can create a projection lock row before an idempotent early return, bypassing maintenance admission.",
      "fix": "Both management paths now check target maintenance immediately after acquiring the model lock and before early returns; real transactions prove the newly inserted projection is rolled back."
    },
    {
      "defect": "The standalone test control transaction manager used DefaultJpaDialect, which cannot apply explicit READ_COMMITTED isolation.",
      "fix": "The real control DB fixture now uses Spring HibernateJpaVendorAdapter properties and JpaDialect, matching platform defaults. Production isolation remains explicit."
    },
    {
      "defect": "A late publish retry during restoration could be recorded as if the restoration itself had failed.",
      "fix": "Direction conflicts are rejected before establishing a failed-batch diagnostic attempt; the durable restoration checkpoint stays unchanged."
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The internal coordinator is verified but not yet connected to public RecordWritePolicyService publish/cancel response, permission, audit and error mapping. The public formula guard remains enabled.",
    "APP trusted definition projection, continued dispatch/recovery, final designer/runtime UI and B1–B5 real business/form/workflow acceptance remain incomplete.",
    "Legacy version-one nonterminal intents have no resource identity snapshot and are refused by the new coordinator rather than silently rewritten; production formula publication has not been enabled. Legacy terminal/storage reads remain compatible.",
    "Real process-kill and lost-response scenarios, wide-model column-split batch input, cross-service broker lifecycle and final upgrade/deployment acceptance remain required.",
    "This batch is not deployed; current DNA remains 20261018-publication-journal1. Earlier stage-storage/maintenance changes also need controlled storage upgrade before taking traffic.",
    "The final 176-entry matrix is not passed. Unrelated previously recorded tenant-module Checkstyle findings remain outstanding."
  ],
